<section class="peter-story">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="story-header">

      <span class="story-label">
        OUR STORY
      </span>

      <h2>
        One Half-Eaten Apple.<br />
        A Lifetime of Compassion.
      </h2>

      <p class="intro">

        Every organisation has a beginning.

        Some begin with funding.

        Others begin with a business plan.

        Compassion Bridge Initiative Uganda began with a hungry little boy,
        half an apple and one unforgettable act of generosity.

      </p>

    </div>

    <div class="story-grid">

      <aside class="story-sidebar">

        <img
          src="/peterstory.png"
          alt="Peter Waiswa"
          class="peter-photo"
        />

        <div class="profile-card">

          <h3>Peter Waiswa</h3>

          <p class="role">

            Founder<br />

            Compassion Bridge Initiative Uganda

          </p>

          <hr />

          <p>

            Accountant by profession.<br />
            Humanitarian by calling.

          </p>

        </div>

      </aside>

      <article class="story-content">

        <span class="chapter">

          CHAPTER ONE

        </span>

        <h3>

          Success Looked Different

        </h3>

        <p>

          Before Compassion Bridge Initiative Uganda existed, Peter Waiswa had
          built a successful career as an accountant in Uganda's banking and
          finance industry.

        </p>

        <p>

          From the outside, life appeared to be moving in the right direction.
          He had a respected profession, a promising future and opportunities
          that many young people dream of.

        </p>

        <p>

          Yet every morning, while driving through Kampala on his way to work,
          he saw another Uganda.

        </p>

        <p>

          Children sleeping on pavements.

          Children begging at traffic lights.

          Children whose tomorrow depended upon the kindness of strangers.

        </p>

        <p>

          He noticed them every day.

          Like many people, he felt sympathy.

          But sympathy had never interrupted his journey.

        </p>

        <span class="chapter">

          CHAPTER TWO

        </span>

        <h3>

          A Traffic Light Changed Everything

        </h3>

        <p>

          One ordinary day in 2018, Peter stopped at a traffic light.

        </p>

        <p>

          As he waited for the signal to change, a young street boy approached
          his window.

        </p>

        <p>

          Quietly and respectfully, the boy asked if Peter could give him some
          money to buy something to eat.

        </p>

        <p>

          Peter smiled sadly and replied,

        </p>

        <blockquote>

          "I don't have any money today.

          In fact...

          I am hungry too."

        </blockquote>

        <p>

          For a brief moment, there was silence.

        </p>

        <p>

          Then the little boy did something Peter would never forget.

        </p>

        <p>

          He reached into his small worn-out bag.

        </p>

        <p>

          Inside was half an apple.

        </p>

        <p>

          Carefully, he stretched it through the car window.

        </p>

        <p>

          Looking Peter in the eyes, he simply said…

        </p>

        <blockquote class="apple-quote">

          "If you are hungry and don't have what to eat…

          don't worry.

          I have got the both of us covered."

        </blockquote>        <p>

          Peter was speechless.

        </p>

        <p>

          The little boy had almost nothing.

          No home.

          No parents.

          No certainty about tomorrow.

          No guarantee of his next meal.

        </p>

        <p>

          Yet he possessed something many people with abundance never discover.

        </p>

        <p>

          He was free to trust.

          Free to love.

          Free to give.

        </p>

        <p>

          That simple act of generosity challenged everything Peter believed
          about success, wealth and purpose.

        </p>

        <p>

          He drove away carrying far more than half an apple.

        </p>

        <p class="highlight">

          He drove away carrying a new calling.

        </p>

        <span class="chapter">

          CHAPTER THREE

        </span>

        <h3>

          Choosing a Different Path

        </h3>

        <p>

          The image of the little boy remained with Peter long after that day.

          He could not forget the child who had almost nothing, yet was willing
          to share everything he had.

        </p>

        <p>

          Slowly, Peter realised that his greatest investment would not be in
          finance, but in people.

        </p>

        <p>

          He made the courageous decision to leave the banking and finance
          industry and dedicate his life to serving vulnerable children and
          communities.

        </p>

        <p>

          This decision led to the establishment of <strong>Such As I Have
          Foundation</strong>, where he began working directly with children
          facing difficult circumstances and families living in poverty.

        </p>

        <p>

          What had begun with one child's unexpected generosity was now
          becoming a life devoted to compassion.

        </p>

        <span class="chapter">

          CHAPTER FOUR

        </span>

        <h3>

          Compassion Became a Movement

        </h3>

        <p>

          Peter's journey later brought him to the
          <strong>Global Compassion Coalition (GCC)</strong>, where he became
          part of the Connectors Program—a global community of people committed
          to serving others through practical acts of compassion.

        </p>

        <p>

          Through this community he formed meaningful friendships with people
          who shared the same vision of restoring dignity and creating
          opportunities for vulnerable communities.

        </p>

        <p>

          Among them was <strong>Tinah</strong>, whose encouragement and
          friendship strengthened the growing vision of building bridges of
          compassion across communities and nations.

        </p>

        <p>

          Peter was later entrusted with serving as the
          <strong>National Coordinator of the Global Compassion Coalition
          Connectors Program in Uganda</strong>, helping connect compassionate
          people and organisations working to create lasting change.

        </p>

        <p>

          Along this journey, many others became part of the vision.

          Among them was <strong>Christine</strong>, whose passion for
          supporting vulnerable children, women and families became an
          important contribution to what would eventually become
          Compassion Bridge Initiative Uganda.

        </p>

        <span class="chapter">

          CHAPTER FIVE

        </span>

        <h3>

          The Story Continues

        </h3>

        <p>

          Today, Compassion Bridge Initiative Uganda works to improve access
          to education, empower women and widows, strengthen livelihoods,
          promote health, develop vocational skills and restore hope to
          vulnerable communities.

        </p>

        <p>

          Every child who remains in school...

        </p>

        <p>

          Every woman who rebuilds her life...

        </p>

        <p>

          Every volunteer who serves...

        </p>

        <p>

          Every partner who walks alongside us...

        </p>

        <p>

          ...is writing the next chapter of this story.

        </p>

        <div class="closing-box">

          <h3>

            The little boy who shared half an apple will probably never know
            how many lives his generosity has touched.

          </h3>

          <p>

            His kindness became the seed of a movement that today continues
            restoring dignity, building brighter futures and creating bridges
            of compassion across Uganda and beyond.

          </p>

        </div>

      </article>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>

